WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.397
SENECA: Incertum est quo loco te mors exspectet. Itaque tu illam omni loco exspecta.

2
00:00:23.197 --> 00:00:25.729
PAULINA: The soldiers have arrived.

3
00:00:28.929 --> 00:00:31.457
SENECA: Then the order has come.

4
00:00:34.857 --> 00:00:38.270
PAULINA: You speak as though you have been waiting for them.

5
00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:46.355
SENECA: I have been waiting for death. Not for the sound of their footsteps.

6
00:00:50.655 --> 00:00:52.827
PAULINA: What happens now?

7
00:00:56.027 --> 00:01:01.613
SENECA: They have given me no choice. But I can choose how to meet it.

8
00:01:04.913 --> 00:01:07.419
PAULINA: Then I will share your fate.

9
00:01:12.019 --> 00:01:14.263
SENECA: I asked you to live.

10
00:01:17.163 --> 00:01:19.975
PAULINA: You asked me to live without you.

11
00:01:23.675 --> 00:01:30.300
SENECA: Vitae delenimenta monstraveram tibi, tu mortis decus mavis.

12
00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:40.090
SENECA: I showed you the consolations of life. You prefer the honour of death.

13
00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:46.812
PAULINA: I do not know how to leave you here alone.

14
00:01:50.912 --> 00:01:53.876
SENECA: Nor do I know how to leave you.

15
00:01:58.776 --> 00:02:00.738
PAULINA: Are you not afraid?

16
00:02:04.238 --> 00:02:09.734
SENECA: Accipio condicionem. Non reformido iudicium.

17
00:02:12.034 --> 00:02:14.782
SENECA: I wrote that before tonight.

18
00:02:18.582 --> 00:02:22.402
SENECA: A sentence is easier to hold than a hand.

19
00:02:28.002 --> 00:02:29.807
PAULINA: Let me stay.

20
00:02:34.807 --> 00:02:38.929
SENECA: Remember my life. Not only this room.

21
00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:45.258
PAULINA: Seneca.
